<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Inapa boosts capital using reserves.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Inapa boosts capital using reserves.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese paper company Inapa said that it would triple its share capital in September by an incorporation of reserves.</p>
<p>Shareholders will not be asked for additional funds in the operation under which they will get two new shares for every share held.</p>
<p>The capital operation will take place in September.  </p>
<p>Inapa said that the main motive of the move was to boost the liquidity of the company's stock on the share market, where it was trading down 30 escudos at 5,700 escudos.</p>
<p>($1=181 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
